Thought: My first evaluation gave 0.789917 with a small 2-layer model, high dropout, low LR. Agent 3 is exploring a large 5-layer model with high LR and low dropout. Agent 1 has a 4-layer model. Agent 0 has the default 3-layer.

I should explore a mid-range config but vary different dimensions. Let me try a moderate-depth model (3 layers) with moderate-to-high capacity, lower dropout, and a slightly higher initial LR than my first attempt, with a different shape parameter. This fills the gap between the small regularized model I tried and the big models others are trying.

